post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

camofox-browser-service installed. Three per-user steps remain — none of them
can be done by a package, because they write under $HOME:

  1. Config (bound to loopback by default — keep it that way):
       install -Dm600 /usr/share/camofox-browser-service/camofox-browser.env.example \
         ~/.config/camofox-browser/camofox-browser.env

  2. Service:
       systemctl --user enable --now camofox-browser
       sudo loginctl enable-linger "$USER"    # survive logout

  3. Agent hosts + skill:
       camofox-kit-register
       install -Dm644 /usr/share/camofox-browser-service/skills/camofox-browser/SKILL.md \
         ~/.claude/skills/camofox-browser/SKILL.md

The REST server itself is NOT in this package. Install one of:
       camofox-browser-bin            (AUR, bundles the browser binary)
       npm install -g @askjo/camofox-browser @askjo/camofox-browser-mcp

Then verify the whole chain:
       camofox-doctor

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'

The unit template was replaced. Reload and restart:
       systemctl --user daemon-reload
       systemctl --user restart camofox-browser

Your ~/.config/camofox-browser/camofox-browser.env was not touched. Compare it
with /usr/share/camofox-browser-service/camofox-browser.env.example for new keys.

EOF
}

pre_remove() {
  # Best-effort: a scriptlet runs as root and cannot reach every user's manager.
  systemctl --user --global disable camofox-browser.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Removed. Left behind on purpose:
       ~/.config/camofox-browser/     config, possibly with keys
       ~/.cache/camoufox/             browser binary (~1.3GB)
       ~/.camofox/                    sessions, cookies, storage state

MCP host entries stay registered until you run:
       camofox-kit-register --remove   (before removing the package)

EOF
}
